    thinking: "**Analyzing Design Components**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the \"Geometric Balance\" design specifications. I\'m focusing on the main container layout, specifically the sidebar. Its components include its width, background color, flexbox attributes, and border styles. The border color is either slate-200 or slate-800. I am breaking down these specifications, to identify their importance.\n\n\n**Detailing UI Elements**\n\nNow, I\'m cataloging specific UI element styles. I\'ve noted the color palettes for menu items, active states, and backgrounds. I\'ve categorized the color codes and Tailwind classes for headers, content cards, headings, and metric displays. I\'ve also made a list of the badge and pill styles and their variations. Lastly, I\'m working through the tables.\n\n\n**Examining Color Consistency**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on color scheme consistency across the application, starting with the tables; the primary focus is to ensure a unified visual experience. I\'ve noted the table row styling, including the use of `border-b` and color classes. Also, the contrast in the AI widget\'s dark gradient panel is pivotal for the overall design balance. Furthermore, I\'m reviewing `MainLayout.tsx`, `Sidebar.tsx`, `Header.tsx`, `DashboardPage.tsx`, and `EmployeesPage`, which are all aligned with Geometric Balance style now.\n\n\n"
