  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Instructions**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s instructions. I\'ve pinpointed the key deliverables: a report, not code modifications, which must include a folder structure analysis. I\'m focusing on the essential components of the request.\n\n\n**Outlining Key Concerns**\n\nI\'ve identified key areas for analysis, from duplicate files and logic to mock data locations and database/API problems. Security and performance are also concerns, as are missing enterprise features. I am thinking about a refactoring roadmap and how to estimate the work in Sprints. The report structure is becoming clearer with each thought!\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "# THEIAKSHI ONE Enterprise HRMS \342\200\224 Architecture & Migration Audit Report\n\n**Project:** THEIAKSHI ONE Enterprise HRMS  \n**Company:** THEIAKSHI ENTERPRISES  \n**Mode:** Architecture Lock Mode \342\200\224 Assessment & Migration Roadmap  \n**Status:** Audit Complete (No code modifications executed)\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nTHEIAKSHI ONE Enterprise HRMS currently features a functional full-stack setup with Express routing, raw SQL repository patterns, clean Tailwind visual layouts, and AI-assisted analytics integration. However, to transition into a **production-grade enterprise architecture**, several core structural, security, database, and API standardization gaps must be systematically addressed.\n\nThis report outlines the complete diagnostic analysis of the codebase along with an actionable 5-Sprint Refactoring Roadmap.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Folder Structure Analysis\n\n### Current Structure\n```\n/ (Root)\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server.ts\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 App.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.css\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 main.tsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 backend/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 controllers/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 database/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 middlewares/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 repositories/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 routes/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 types/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 utils/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 layout/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 contexts/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 pages/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 types/\n```\n\n### Analysis & Misalignments\n* **Backend Location inside `/src`:** The backend source files reside under `/src/backend`. In an enterprise monorepo or standard layered backend architecture, server code should be distinctly separated into `/backend/src` or modular server components to isolate client Vite bundling boundaries from server execution.\n* **Frontend Modules Missing:** The frontend currently mixes all feature pages inside a flat `/src/pages` folder without modular decomposition (`/src/modules/attendance`, `/src/modules/payroll`, etc.).\n* **Absence of Infrastructure Layers:** Missing `socket`, `jobs` (cron background jobs for attendance/payroll auto-generation), `events`, `storage` (S3/Cloud Storage receipt file upload), and `mail` (SMTP/Nodemailer for payslip & leave approval emails) sub-directories in backend architecture.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Duplicate Files Analysis\n\n* **`apiClient.ts` vs inline Axios/Fetch instances:** `/src/services/apiClient.ts` is configured with request interceptors for JWT, but individual components occasionally re-declare query states or bypass centralized error handling.\n* **Type Declarations Fragmentation:** Shared interfaces (`Employee`, `Attendance`, `Leave`, `Payroll`) are split across `/src/types/index.ts` (Frontend types) and `/src/backend/types/index.ts` (Backend DTOs). These should be standardized in a shared contract layer.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Duplicate Logic Analysis\n\n* **SQL Column Mapping & Result Mapping:** Repositories (`employeeRepository`, `attendanceRepository`, `payrollRepository`) repeat manual parameter arrays and manual column mapping logic for pagination, date formatting, and filter assembly.\n* **JWT Token Verification:** Authorization bearer header extraction and validation logic is duplicated across custom middleware and inline controller handlers.\n* **Response Envelope Construction:** `res.json({ success: true, data: ... })` vs `res.json({ status: \'ok\', ... })` envelope structures are inconsistently created in different controller methods rather than using a unified response formatter utility.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Mock Data Locations & In-Memory Data Audit\n\n* **Embedded WASM Engine Seed (`/src/backend/database/seed.ts`):** Contains extensive static fallback arrays for initial startup (mock employees, default department records, mock leave balances, demo expense receipts, sample projects).\n* **`PGlite` In-Memory Storage (`/src/backend/database/db.ts`):** Currently leverages `@electric-sql/pglite` (WASM in-memory/ephemeral instance). Data written during execution is reset when the server container restarts.\n* **Hardcoded Geofence Distance Fallback:** Geofence distance calculation in `AttendancePage.tsx` falls back to hardcoded `64m` or mock GPS coordinates when location permission or real hardware sensors are offline.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Database Architectural Problems\n\n* **WASM/PGlite Ephemeral DB:** The application is running an embedded WASM database instance rather than a persistent pooled Neon PostgreSQL connection (`pg` / `pg-pool`).\n* **Lack of Migration Management:** Schema changes in `/src/backend/database/schema.ts` rely on `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` raw SQL scripts rather than a strict database migration framework (e.g., Drizzle ORM / Kysely / Prisma / Flyway).\n* **Missing Indexing & Foreign Key Cascades:** Tables lack optimized indexing on foreign key joins (`tenant_id`, `employee_id`, `department_id`) and timestamps (`punch_in`, `start_date`), leading to full-table scans under enterprise loads.\n* **No Connection Pooling / Health Check Circuit Breaker:** Absence of retry mechanisms or connection pool limits for cloud DB connections.\n\n---\n\n## 6. API Standard & Structure Inconsistencies\n\n* **Response Envelope Deviation:** Some endpoints return raw arrays or plain objects (`res.json([...])`), while others return `{ status: \'ok\', ... }`. Standard constraint mandates `{ success: boolean, message: string, data: any }`.\n* **Monolithic API Router:** All routes are registered in a single `/src/backend/routes/api.ts` file rather than split into feature-specific router files (`attendance.routes.ts`, `payroll.routes.ts`, `leave.routes.ts`).\n* **HTTP Status Code Uniformity:** Error responses occasionally use 200 OK with error messages inside the body instead of proper HTTP status codes (400, 401, 403, 404, 500).\n\n---\n\n## 7. Security Issues\n\n* **Static JWT Secret Fallback:** Default fallback secret key hardcoded in environment utilities when `JWT_SECRET` is undefined.\n* **Missing Rate Limiting:** No Express rate limiters (`express-rate-limit`) on sensitive authentication (`/api/v1/auth/login`) or punch endpoints.\n* **Lack of Request Payload Sanitization & Validation:** Missing schema validation middlewares (e.g., Zod / Joi) on incoming request bodies, exposing SQL string inputs or invalid payload formats.\n* **CORS Wildcard Configuration:** CORS is enabled with permissive defaults (`app.use(cors())`).\n\n---\n\n## 8. Performance Issues\n\n* **Unbounded Database Queries:** Queries in `employeeRepository` and `attendanceRepository` lack required `LIMIT` and `OFFSET` clauses, risking memory spikes when data exceeds thousands of records.\n* **Server-Side File Bundle Size:** Bundled static assets served directly through Vite middleware without HTTP compression (`compression` Express middleware) or cache-control headers.\n* **State Re-render Hotspots:** React components make direct multi-fetch requests on every tab mount rather than caching query results via global state management or React Query/SWR patterns.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Missing Enterprise Features\n\n* **Multi-Tenant Isolation:** Database tables lack tenant ID isolation (`tenant_id`) for multi-entity corporate deployments.\n* **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):** Granular permission checks (Admin, HR Manager, Department Head, Employee) are not enforced on backend API endpoints.\n* **Audit Logging Engine:** System activity, salary changes, leave approvals, and manual punch overrides are not recorded in an immutable `audit_logs` database table.\n* **Background Job Scheduler:** Automated month-end payroll processing, daily auto-checkout for unpunched employees, and entitlement accrual crons are missing.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Refactoring Roadmap\n\n```\nPhase 1: Database & Foundation (Sprint 1)\n  \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Migrate PGlite to Neon PostgreSQL pool, standard response formatter, environment validation.\n\nPhase 2: Layered Architecture & Repositories (Sprint 2)\n  \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Isolate Repositories, Services, and Controllers. Enforce strictly zero SQL in controllers/services.\n\nPhase 3: Frontend Refactoring & Isolation (Sprint 3)\n  \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Reorganize into /src/modules, isolate all API requests inside service layer, enforce uniform UI tokens.\n\nPhase 4: Security, RBAC & Enterprise Audit (Sprint 4)\n  \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Implement Zod schema validation, JWT auth middleware, Rate Limiting, RBAC permissions, Audit Logger.\n\nPhase 5: Automated Crons, Notifications & PDF Engine (Sprint 5)\n  \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Implement background jobs, email notifications, PDF payslip generator, and multi-tenant isolation.\n```\n\n---\n\n## 11. Estimated Work in Sprints\n\n### Sprint 1: Core Database & Infrastructure Hardening\n* **Goal:** Replace in-memory PGlite with persistent Neon PostgreSQL pool and establish uniform API envelope formatting.\n* **Tasks:**\n  1. Configure `pg` pool in `/src/backend/database/db.ts` utilizing existing PostgreSQL environment strings.\n  2. Implement global API Response utility returning `{ success, message, data }`.\n  3. Decompose monolithic `api.ts` into modular route files (`auth.routes.ts`, `employee.routes.ts`, `attendance.routes.ts`, `payroll.routes.ts`, `leave.routes.ts`).\n  4. Add centralized Express error handling middleware.\n\n### Sprint 2: Backend Architecture & Business Logic Decoupling\n* **Goal:** Enforce strict separation: Controllers $\\rightarrow$ Services $\\rightarrow$ Repositories $\\rightarrow$ SQL Execution.\n* **Tasks:**\n  1. Move all business logic out of controllers into dedicated service classes (`AttendanceService`, `PayrollService`, `LeaveService`).\n  2. Verify repositories strictly handle parameterized SQL queries without leaking domain logic.\n  3. Ensure no SQL statements exist inside controllers or services.\n  4. Add standard pagination wrappers (`{ limit, page, total, items }`) across all listing queries.\n\n### Sprint 3: Modular Frontend Refactoring & API Isolation\n* **Goal:** Refactor client application into modular directory layout with 100% isolated API communication.\n* **Tasks:**\n  1. Restructure frontend into `/src/modules/` (e.g., `attendance`, `payroll`, `employees`, `leave`, `projects`).\n  2. Create typed service files for every domain (`attendanceService.ts`, `payrollService.ts`) wrapping `apiClient`.\n  3. Eliminate direct fetch calls inside React components.\n  4. Implement global toast notification and loading state handlers.\n\n### Sprint 4: Enterprise Security, RBAC & Audit Logging\n* **Goal:** Enforce security policies, rate limits, input validation, and audit tracking.\n* **Tasks:**\n  1. Integrate Zod request validation schemas for all POST/PUT/PATCH endpoints.\n  2. Implement granular RBAC middleware (`checkPermission(\'MANAGE_PAYROLL\')`, `checkPermission(\'APPROVE_LEAVE\')`).\n  3. Create `audit_logs` database table and append events on critical mutations (payroll disbursement, leave approval, employee status change).\n  4. Apply Express rate-limiting on authentication and sensitive endpoints.\n\n### Sprint 5: Enterprise Automation, Crons & Multi-Tenancy\n* **Goal:** Deliver production background services, automated notifications, and multi-entity support.\n* **Tasks:**\n  1. Integrate background job queue/cron runner for automated daily punch-out and monthly payroll calculations.\n  2. Implement server-side PDF generation for itemized salary payslips.\n  3. Add `tenant_id` column constraints across all tables for enterprise multi-tenancy.\n  4. Final end-to-end integration test suite and performance optimization.\n\n---\n\n### Confirmation\n**Architecture Lock Mode is Active.** No codebase files were edited during this audit turn. Awaiting your signal to proceed with Sprint 1 implementation."
    thinking_duration {
