  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Scope and Constraints**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining the precise scope of this enterprise HRMS blueprint and migration roadmap. My primary focus remains strictly non-code-related, as per the instructions. I\'m also carefully considering the limitations imposed on execution. This focus is providing a clearer direction on the key elements to incorporate.\n\n\n**Refining Output Structure**\n\nI\'m now meticulously structuring the response, ensuring comprehensive coverage and executive presentation. I\'m focusing on organizing all required sections with utmost clarity. The migration report and analysis will be structured to identify and address concerns, including duplicate elements and missing features. I\'m carefully considering the folder structure analysis, duplicate files, mock data removal, and database and security aspects. The target enterprise architecture design will include a complete folder tree, database architecture, module dependency diagrams, and API architecture with standardized responses.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "# THEIAKSHI ONE ENTERPRISE HRMS\n## Enterprise Software Architecture Blueprint & Production Migration Roadmap\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 1: ARCHITECTURE ANALYSIS & MIGRATION REPORT\n\n### 1. Folder Structure Analysis\n* **Current State**: The repository features an Express backend located inside `src/backend/` and a React Vite frontend in `src/`. Server setup resides in `/server.ts`.\n* **Identified Issues**:\n  * Frontend components (`src/pages/*`) currently issue direct HTTP calls via inline `fetch` or use `apiClient.ts` inconsistently.\n  * Backend routing is centralized into a single `/src/backend/routes/api.ts` monolith rather than modularized routes per domain.\n  * Shared types are loosely spread across `src/types/` and `src/backend/types/`.\n\n### 2. Duplicate Files, Logic & Services\n* **Database Access**: A single `db.ts` file manages Neon PostgreSQL connection pool using `pg`. No duplicate database helpers exist.\n* **Controllers & Repositories**: High cohesion exists in repositories (`employeeRepository.ts`, `attendanceRepository.ts`, `payrollRepository.ts`, etc.), but controller handling in `miscController.ts` aggregates multiple unrelated domains (Expenses, Leaves, Projects, Assets, Announcements, Helpdesk).\n\n### 3. Mock Data Locations & Elimination Strategy\n* **Mock Objects Found**:\n  * `DashboardPage.tsx`: Static fallback array for announcements and celebrations when backend payloads are empty.\n  * `AttendancePage.tsx`: Hardcoded geofence coordinates (`12.9279\302\260 N, 77.6892\302\260 E`) and fallback distance calculations.\n* **Elimination Strategy**: All mock fallbacks will be removed in favor of strict PostgreSQL queries with default database seed records populated via `seed.ts`.\n\n### 4. Database, API, Security & Performance Analysis\n* **Database**: Neon PostgreSQL connection pooling (`pg.Pool`) configured with ssl mode enabled. SQL queries use parameterized placeholders (`$1, $2`), preventing SQL injection.\n* **API Standardization**: APIs currently mix raw JSON outputs and standardized payloads. All endpoints will enforce the strict standard `{ success: boolean, message: string, data: T }`.\n* **Security & Auth**: JWT verification middleware is present in `/src/backend/middlewares/authMiddleware.ts`. Passwords use `bcryptjs` hashing. CSRF headers and rate-limiting require enforcement.\n* **Performance**: Missing database indexes on foreign keys (`employee_id`, `tenant_id`, `branch_id`, `punch_in`) will be addressed in schema migrations.\n\n### 5. Missing Enterprise Features\n* Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) granular permission guards (e.g., `HR_ADMIN`, `BRANCH_MANAGER`, `EMPLOYEE`).\n* Multi-tenant data segregation (`tenant_id` columns across all tables).\n* Centralized audit logging table (`audit_logs`) tracking model mutations.\n* Background queue worker for async operations (PDF generation, payroll batch calculation).\n* WebSocket support for real-time notification broadcasting.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Refactoring Roadmap (Sprint 1 to 5)\n\n```\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                        5-SPRINT REFACTORING TIMELINE                              |\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| SPRINT 1 | Core Foundation, Modular Directory Restructure & Database Indexes      |\n| SPRINT 2 | API Standardization, Service-Repository Decoupling & RBAC Guards        |\n| SPRINT 3 | Core HR Modules Migration (Employees, Attendance, Leave, Payroll)      |\n| SPRINT 4 | Operational Modules (Expense, Recruitment, Projects, Assets, Helpdesk) |\n| SPRINT 5 | Real-Time Sockets, Firebase FCM, AI Assistant & Mobile API Layer         |\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n* **Sprint 1: Architecture & Structural Foundation**\n  * Establish clean separation between `backend/src/` and `src/`.\n  * Modularize backend routes (`/routes/v1/*.ts`).\n  * Add DB indexes for foreign keys, composite search fields, and timestamp ranges.\n* **Sprint 2: Security, RBAC & API Normalization**\n  * Standardize all Express controller responses to `{ success, message, data }`.\n  * Enforce RBAC permission middleware on all endpoints.\n  * Centralize frontend HTTP communications into domain-specific services (`/src/services/*.ts`).\n* **Sprint 3: Core Employee & Financial Workflows**\n  * Refactor Employee Directory, Attendance GPS Geofencing, Leave Approvals, and Payroll Engine.\n  * Integrate PDF generation service for Itemized Payslip downloads.\n* **Sprint 4: Enterprise Operations & Support Systems**\n  * Migrate Reimbursement Claims, ATS Recruitment, Project Delivery, IT Hardware Assets, and Helpdesk Tickets.\n  * Integrate Cloudinary SDK for receipt and document attachments.\n* **Sprint 5: Real-Time Sockets, AI Engine & Production Readiness**\n  * Mount Socket.io real-time layer for instant notification toasts.\n  * Proxy server-side Gemini 3.6 Flash for natural language HR Analytics.\n  * Mobile API optimization and Neon PostgreSQL connection tuning.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 2: TARGET ENTERPRISE ARCHITECTURE DESIGN\n\n### 1. Complete Folder Tree\n\n```\n/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 .env.example\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 package.json\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 tsconfig.json\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 vite.config.ts\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server.ts\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 backend/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 config/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 env.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 postgres.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 cloudinary.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 firebase.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 database/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 db.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 schema.sql\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 seed.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 controllers/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 authController.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 employeeController.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 attendanceController.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 leaveController.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 payrollController.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 expenseController.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 recruitmentController.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 projectController.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 assetController.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 documentController.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 helpdeskController.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 notificationController.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 dashboardController.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 aiController.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 reportController.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 authService.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\2