24\200\342\224\200 events/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 eventEmitter.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 storage/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 cloudinaryStorage.ts\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 mail/\n\342\224\202           \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 mailer.ts\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 main.tsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 App.tsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.css\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 common/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Button.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Card.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Modal.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Table.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 layout/\n    \342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Header.tsx\n    \342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 MainLayout.tsx\n    \342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Sidebar.tsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 modules/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 employees/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 attendance/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 payroll/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 leaves/\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 pages/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 DashboardPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 EmployeesPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 AttendancePage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 LeavePage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 PayrollPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ExpensesPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 RecruitmentPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ProjectsPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 OrgChartPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 HelpdeskPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 WeeklyPlannerPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 LoginPage.tsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 hooks/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 useAuth.ts\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 useNotifications.ts\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 useSocket.ts\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 apiClient.ts\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 employeeService.ts\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 attendanceService.ts\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 leaveService.ts\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 payrollService.ts\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 aiService.ts\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 contexts/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 AuthContext.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 SocketContext.tsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 routes/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 AppRoutes.tsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 utils/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 formatters.ts\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 dateUtils.ts\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 types/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.ts\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 theme/\n        \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 colors.ts\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Database Architecture (Neon PostgreSQL)\n\nThe database runs on Neon Serverless PostgreSQL using native `pg` connection pool with SSL configured.\n\n```\n+------------------+         +---------------------+         +-------------------+\n|    tenants       |1       *|     branches        |1       *|    departments    |\n+------------------+---------+---------------------+---------+-------------------+\n| id (PK)          |         | id (PK)             |         | id (PK)           |\n| name             |         | tenant_id (FK)      |         | tenant_id (FK)    |\n| domain           |         | name, geofence_lat  |         | branch_id (FK)    |\n+------------------+         | geofence_lng, radius|         | name              |\n                             +---------------------+         +-------------------+\n                                        |                             |\n                                        +--------------+--------------+\n                                                       |1\n                                                       |*\n                                             +-------------------+\n                                             |     employees     |\n                                             +-------------------+\n                                             | id (PK)           |\n                                             | tenant_id (FK)    |\n                                             | branch_id (FK)    |\n                                             | department_id (FK)|\n                                             | employee_code     |\n                                             | email, password_hash|\n                                             | role (ADMIN/EMP)  |\n                                             +-------------------+\n                                                       |\n        +------------------+------------------+--------+--------+-------------------+\n        |1                 |1                 |1                |1                  |1\n        |*                 |*                 |*                |*                  |*\n+---------------+  +---------------+  +---------------+  +---------------+  +---------------+\n|  attendance   |  | leave_requests|  | payroll_slips |  |    expenses   |  |   helpdesk    |\n+---------------+  +---------------+  +---------------+  +---------------+  +---------------+\n| id (PK)       |  | id (PK)       |  | id (PK)       |  | id (PK)       |  | id (PK)       |\n| employee_id   |  | employee_id   |  | employee_id   |  | employee_id   |  | employee_id   |\n| punch_in      |  | start_date    |  | month, year   |  | amount        |  | ticket_code   |\n| punch_out     |  | end_date      |  | gross_salary  |  | receipt_url   |  | priority      |\n| gps_lat, lng  |  | status        |  | net_salary    |  | status        |  | status        |\n+---------------+  +---------------+  +---------------+  +---------------+  +---------------+\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Module Dependency Diagram\n\n```\n                       +------------------------+\n                       |   Core Auth & RBAC     |\n                       +------------------------+\n                                   |\n           +-----------------------+-----------------------+\n           |                                               |\n           v                                               v\n+------------------------+                       +------------------------+\n|    Employees Core      |                       |  Branches & Geofences  |\n+------------------------+                       +------------------------+\n           |                                               |\n     +-----+-----+-------------------+---------------------+-----+\n     |           |                   |                     |     |\n     v           v                   v                     v     v\n+----------+ +-------+       +---------------+       +----------+ +-----------+\n|Attendance| | Leaves|       | Payroll Engine|       | Expenses | | Helpdesk  |\n+----------+ +-------+       +---------------+       +----------+ +-----------+\n     |           |                   |                     |         |\n     +-----------+---------+---------+---------------------+---------+\n                           |\n                           v\n              +--------------------------+\n              | Enterprise Dashboard & AI|\n              +--------------------------+\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. API Architecture & Standard Response Format\n\nAll HTTP API endpoints adhere strictly to the uniform response envelope:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"message\": \"Operation completed successfully\",\n  \"data\": { ... }\n}\n```\n\nIn case of error, the payload returns:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": false,\n  \"message\": \"Validation failed / Unauthorized access\",\n  \"data\": null\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Authentication Flow\n\n```\n[ Client App ] --( 1. POST /api/auth/login {email, password} )--> [ Auth Controller ]\n                                                                          |\n                                                              2. Verify Hash via bcrypt\n                                                                          |\n[ Client App ] <--( 3. Return JWT Token in Standard JSON Envelope )-------+\n      |\n ( 4. Subsequent requests attached in header: \"Authorization: Bearer <JWT>\" )\n      |\n      v\n[ Auth Middleware ] ---> Decodes Token ---> Attaches user object to `req.user`\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) Design\n\nPermissions are defined by role hierarchy:\n* **SUPER_ADMIN**: Global cross-tenant access.\n* **HR_ADMIN**: Tenant-wide management (Employees, Payroll, Leaves, Expenses).\n* **BRANCH_MANAGER**: Branch-specific scope for Attendance approvals and Leave sign-offs.\n* **EMPLOYEE**: Self-service access (Punch in/out, view own payslips, submit reimbursement claims).\n\nMiddleware pattern:\n```typescript\n// backend/src/middlewares/rbacMiddleware.ts\nexport const requireRole = (allowedRoles: string[]) => {\n  return (req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction) => {\n    if (!req.user || !allowedRoles.includes(req.user.role)) {\n      return res.status(403).json({\n        success: false,\n        message: \'Access denied: Insufficient privileges\',\n        data: null\n      });\n    }\n    next();\n  };\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. Audit Logging Flow\n\n1. Any write operation in a repository (`INSERT`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`) invokes `auditRepository.logAction()`.\n2. Captured attributes: `tenant_id`, `actor_id`, `action`, `entity_type`, `entity_id`, `old_values` (JSONB), `new_values` (JSONB), `ip_address`, `timestamp`.\n3. Non-blocking asynchronous insertion ensures zero impact on primary database query latencies.\n\n---\n\n### 8. Notification Flow\n\n```\n[ Trigger Event (e.g. Leave Approved) ]\n                  |\n                  v\n       [ Notification Service ]\n                  |\n        +---------+---------+\n        |                   |\n        v                   v\n[ Save to DB ]      [ Socket Manager Broadcast ]\n (In-app Feed)       (Instant Browser Toast)\n                            |\n                            v\n                    [ Firebase FCM Push ]\n                     (Mobile Devices)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 9. Background Jobs Architecture\n\n* **Cron Engine**: Managed via Node.js internal interval timer / node-cron in `cronScheduler.ts`.\n* **Scheduled Tasks**:\n  * **Daily 00:01 AM**: Generate default daily attendance ledger records for active employees.\n  * **Monthly 1st 02:00 AM**: Auto-calculate monthly accruals for Leave Balances.\n  * **Payroll Batch Run**: Asynchronously process salary slips and emit PDF generation jobs.\n\n---\n\n### 10. Socket Real-Time Architecture\n\n* Built using `Socket.io` attached to the Express HTTP Server instance in `server.ts`.\n* Authenticated using JWT handshake tokens.\n* Users join channel rooms based on their `tenant_id` and `employee_id`.\n* Enables real-time punch status broadcasts, emergency announcements, and live helpdesk updates.\n\n---\n\n### 11. Shared Types Strategy\n\nTypes are defined in `src/types/index.ts` and imported by both backend controllers and frontend services to guarantee end-to-end type safety.\n\n```typescript\nexport interface ApiResponse<T> {\n  success: boolean;\n  message: string;\n  data: T;\n}\n\nexport interface UserDTO {\n  id: number;\n  tenant_id: number;\n  email: string;\n  first_name: string;\n  last_name: string;\n  role: \'SUPER_ADMIN\' | \'HR_ADMIN\' | \'BRANCH_MANAGER\' | \'EMPLOYEE\';\n  branch_id?: number;\n  department_id?: number;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 12. Frontend Architecture (React 18 + Services Layer)\n\n* **UI Layer**: React Functional Components, styled with Tailwind CSS, Lucide Icons, and Motion animations.\n* **State Management**: React Context (`AuthContext`, `SocketContext`) for global states; local state for views.\n* **Services Layer**: Pure API service modules (`employeeService.ts`, `attendanceService.ts`) wrapping `apiClient.ts` (Axios / Fetch) to shield UI components from HTTP details.\n\n---\n\n### 13. Backend Architecture (Layered Architecture)\n\n```\n[ HTTP Request ] \342\224\200\342\224\200> [ Route Layer ] \342\224\200\342\224\200> [ Middleware (Auth / RBAC) ]\n                                                   \342\224\202\n                                                   \342\226\274\n[ Repositories (SQL Queries) ] <\342\224\200\342\224\200 [ Services (Business Logic) ] <\342\224\200\342\224\200 [ Controllers (Validation & Response) ]\n           \342\224\202\n           \342\226\274\n[ Neon PostgreSQL DB ]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 14. Deployment Architecture\n\n* **Application Hosting**: Google Cloud Run / Render Container Instance running Node.js server.\n* **Database Hosting**: Neon Serverless PostgreSQL with auto-scaling compute and connection pooling.\n* **Static Assets & Uploads**: Cloudinary CDN for attachments, receipts, and avatars.\n* **SSL & Ingress**: Managed reverse proxy routing Port 3000.\n\n---\n\n### 15. Render Deployment Configuration\n\n```yaml\n# render.yaml\nservices:\n  - type: web\n    name: theiakshi-one-hrms\n    env: node\n    buildCommand: npm run build\n    startCommand: npm start\n    envVars:\n      - key: NODE_ENV\n        value: production\n      - key: PORT\n        value: 3000\n      - key: DATABASE_URL\n        fromDatabase:\n          name: neon-postgres\n          property: connectionString\n```\n\n---\n\n### 16. Neon PostgreSQL Production Pooling Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// backend/src/config/postgres.ts\nimport { Pool } from \'pg\';\n\nexport const pool = new Pool({\n  connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL,\n  ssl: { rejectUnauthorized: false },\n  max: 20, // Max concurrent connections in pool\n  idleTimeoutMillis: 30000,\n  connectionTimeoutMillis: 5000,\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 17. Cloudinary Asset & Attachment Storage Integration\n\n* **Configuration**: `cloudinary.v2` initialized with `CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME`, `CLOUDINARY_API_KEY`, and `CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET`.\n* **Usage**: Expense reimbursement receipts, candidate resume PDFs, and employee profile pictures uploaded directly to Cloudinary via server-side middleware, returning HTTPS URLs stored in PostgreSQL.\n\n---\n\n### 18. Firebase Push Notification Flow\n\n* Firebase Admin SDK initialized on backend via service account credentials.\n* Device FCM registration tokens collected on user login and stored in `user_device_tokens` table.\n* Notification Service sends FCM payloads for urgent events (e.g. Leave Approval, Payroll Disbursal).\n\n---\n\n### 19. AI Integration Architecture (Server-Side Gemini Proxy)\n\n```\n[ React AI Brief Widget ] \342\224\200\342\224\200( POST /api/ai/brief )\342\224\200\342\224\200> [ AI Controller ]\n                                                             \342\224\202\n                                                             \342\226\274\n                                                    [ AI Service ]\n                                                             \342\224\202\n                                     ( Fetches Live Aggregated HR Stats from Repositories )\n                                                             \342\224\202\n                                                             \342\226\274\n                                                [ @google/genai SDK ]\n                                              ( Gemini 3.6 Flash Engine )\n                                                             \342\224\202\n[ Formatted Executive Brief ] <\342\224\200\342\224\200 ( JSON Response ) \342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n```\n\n---\n\n### 20. File Upload Architecture\n\n* Express backend uses `multer` middleware in memory (`multer.memoryStorage()`).\n* Upload stream piped directly to Cloudinary or stored securely in DB as base64/URL reference.\n* PDF downloads (e.g. Payslips) generated on-the-fly using `pdfkit` / `jspdf` and streamed to the client response with headers `Content-Type: application/pdf`.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 3: MODULE-BY-MODULE DEVELOPMENT ROADMAP\n\n```\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                           15-MODULE EXECUTION ORDER                               |\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| 1. Employees    2. Attendance    3. Leave         4. Payroll        5. Expense    |\n| 6. Recruitment  7. Projects      8. Assets        9. Documents     10. Helpdesk   |\n| 11. Notifications 12. Dashboard  13. AI Assistant 14. Mobile API   15. Reports    |\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n---\n\n### Module 1: Employees Core\n* **Tables**: `employees`, `departments`, `branches`, `emergency_contacts`, `bank_details`.\n* **APIs**:\n  * `GET /api/v1/employees` - List all active employees\n  * `POST /api/v1/employees` - Create employee record\n  * `GET /api/v1/employees/:id` - Get employee profile detail\n  * `PUT /api/v1/employees/:id` - Update profile\n  * `DELETE /api/v1/employees/:id` - Soft delete employee\n* **Controllers**: `employeeController.ts`\n* **Services**: `employeeService.ts`\n* **Repositories**: `employeeRepository.ts`\n* **React Pages**: `EmployeesPage.tsx`, `OrgChartPage.tsx`\n* **Components**: `EmployeeTable.tsx`, `EmployeeModal.tsx`, `ProfileCard.tsx`\n* **Estimated Files**: 9 files\n* **Dependencies**: `bcryptjs`, `lucide-react`\n\n---\n\n### Module 2: Attendance & GPS Geofencing\n* **Tables**: `attendance_logs`, `geofence_zones`, `shift_schedules`.\n* **APIs**:\n  * `POST /api/v1/attendance/punch-in` - Record punch with lat/lng validation\n  * `POST /api/v1/attendance/punch-out` - Record punch out\n  * `GET /api/v1/attendance/today` - Today\'s attendance stream across company\n  * `GET /api/v1/attendance/my-history` - Employee personal logs\n* **Controllers**: `attendanceController.ts`\n* **Services**: `attendanceService.ts`\n* **Repositories**: `attendanceRepository.ts`\n* **React Pages**: `AttendancePage.tsx`\n* **Components**: `PunchWidget.tsx`, `LiveAttendanceStream.tsx`, `GeofenceMap.tsx`\n* **Estimated Files**: 7 files\n* **Dependencies**: `@turf/distance` (or Haversine formula helper)\n\n---\n\n### Module 3: Leave & Time-Off Management\n* **Tables**: `leave_types`, `leave_balances`, `leave_requests`.\n* **APIs**:\n  * `GET /api/v1/leaves/balances` - Fetch user leave entitlement balances\n  * `POST /api/v1/leaves/apply` - Submit leave request\n  * `PUT /api/v1/leaves/:id/status` - Approve/Reject leave application\n  * `GET /api/v1/leaves/all` - Manager view of all pending leaves\n* **Controllers**: `leaveController.ts`\n* **Services**: `leaveService.ts`\n* **Repositories**: `leaveRepository.ts`\n* **React Pages**: `LeavePage.tsx`\n* **Components**: `LeaveBalanceCard.tsx`, `LeaveApplyModal.tsx`, `LeaveRequestsTable.tsx`\n* **Estimated Files**: 7 files\n* **Dependencies**: `date-fns`\n\n---\n\n### Module 4: Payroll & Itemized Payslips\n* **Tables**: `payroll_slips`, `salary_structures`, `statutory_rates` (PF/ESI/TDS).\n* **APIs**:\n  * `GET /api/v1/payroll/history` - Monthly payroll disbursements list\n  * `GET /api/v1/payroll/payslip/:id` - Fetch itemized payslip details\n  * `POST /api/v1/payroll/generate` - Trigger monthly batch payroll calculation\n* **Controllers**: `payrollController.ts`\n* **Services**: `payrollService.ts`\n* **Repositories**: `payrollRepository.ts`\n* **React Pages**: `PayrollPage.tsx`\n* **Components**: `PayslipModal.tsx`, `PayrollTable.tsx`, `SalaryBreakdown.tsx`\n* **Estimated Files**: 8 files\n* **Dependencies**: `jspdf` / `html2canvas`\n\n---\n\n### Module 5: Expense Reimbursements\n* **Tables**: `expense_claims`, `expense_categories`.\n* **APIs**:\n  * `GET /api/v1/expenses` - List submitted expense claims\n  * `POST /api/v1/expenses` - Submit new reimbursement claim with receipt\n  * `PUT /api/v1/expenses/:id/status` - Approve/Reject claim\n* **Controllers**: `expenseController.ts`\n* **Services**: `expenseService.ts`\n* **Repositories**: `expenseRepository.ts`\n* **React Pages**: `ExpensesPage.tsx`\n* **Components**: `ExpenseClaimModal.tsx`, `ExpenseTable.tsx`\n* **Estimated Files**: 6 files\n* **Dependencies**: `cloudinary`\n\n---\n\n### Module 6: Recruitment & ATS Pipeline\n* **Tables**: `job_requisitions`, `candidates`, `interview_schedules`.\n* **APIs**:\n  * `GET /api/v1/recruitment/jobs` - List open requisitions\n  * `POST /api/v1/recruitment/jobs` - Create new job posting\n  * `GET /api/v1/recruitment/candidates` - Candidate ATS pipeline view\n* **Controllers**: `recruitmentController.ts`\n* **Services**: `recruitmentService.ts`\n* **Repositories**: `recruitmentRepository.ts`\n* **React Pages**: `RecruitmentPage.tsx`\n* **Components**: `JobCard.tsx`, `CandidatePipelineBoard.tsx`\n* **Estimated Files**: 6 files\n* **Dependencies**: `lucide-react`\n\n---\n\n### Module 7: Projects & Task Delivery\n* **Tables**: `projects`, `project_members`, `project_tasks`.\n* **APIs**:\n  * `GET /api/v1/projects` - List active enterprise client projects\n  * `POST /api/v1/projects` - Create new project\n  * `GET /api/v1/projects/:id/tasks` - Fetch project task status\n* **Controllers**: `projectController.ts`\n* **Services**: `projectService.ts`\n* **Repositories**: `projectRepository.ts`\n* **React Pages**: `ProjectsPage.tsx`\n* **Components**: `ProjectProgressCard.tsx`, `TaskBoard.tsx`\n* **Estimated Files**: 6 files\n* **Dependencies**: `recharts`\n\n---\n\n### Module 8: IT Assets & Hardware Tracking\n* **Tables**: `assets`, `asset_allocations`.\n* **APIs**:\n  * `GET /api/v1/assets` - List IT assets inventory\n  * `POST /api/v1/assets/allocate` - Assign hardware to employee\n* **Controllers**: `assetController.ts`\n* **Services**: `assetService.ts`\n* **Repositories**: `assetRepository.ts`\n* **React Pages**: `RecruitmentPage.tsx` (Sub-tab) / Dedicated Assets View\n* **Components**: `AssetTable.tsx`\n* **Estimated Files**: 4 files\n* **Dependencies**: `lucide-react`\n\n---\n\n### Module 9: Enterprise Documents Repository\n* **Tables**: `documents`, `document_folders`, `document_access`.\n* **APIs**:\n  * `GET /api/v1/documents` - Fetch company policy & contract documents\n  * `POST /api/v1/documents/upload` - Secure upload to Cloudinary\n* **Controllers**: `documentController.ts`\n* **Services**: `documentService.ts`\n* **Repositories**: `documentRepository.ts`\n* **React Pages**: `DocumentsPage.tsx`\n* **Components**: `DocumentExplorer.tsx`, `FileUploadZone.tsx`\n* **Estimated Files**: 5 files\n* **Dependencies**: `cloudinary`, `multer`\n\n---\n\n### Module 10: Support Helpdesk & Ticketing\n* **Tables**: `helpdesk_tickets`, `ticket_replies`.\n* **APIs**:\n  * `GET /api/v1/helpdesk/tickets` - List open support tickets\n  * `POST /api/v1/helpdesk/tickets` - Create new ticket\n  * `PUT /api/v1/helpdesk/tickets/:id` - Resolve or update priority\n* **Controllers**: `helpdeskController.ts`\n* **Services**: `helpdeskService.ts`\n* **Repositories**: `helpdeskRepository.ts`\n* **React Pages**: `HelpdeskPage.tsx`\n* **Components**: `TicketTable.tsx`, `TicketModal.tsx`\n* **Estimated Files**: 5 files\n* **Dependencies**: `lucide-react`\n\n---\n\n### Module 11: Enterprise Notifications & Announcements\n* **Tables**: `notifications`, `announcements`, `celebrations`.\n* **APIs**:\n  * `GET /api/v1/notifications` - Unread user notifications\n  * `POST /api/v1/notifications/mark-read` - Clear notification badge\n  * `GET /api/v1/announcements` - Corporate broadcasts list\n* **Controllers**: `notificationController.ts`\n* **Services**: `notificationService.ts`\n* **Repositories**: `notificationRepository.ts`\n* **React Pages**: Integrated in `Header.tsx` & `DashboardPage.tsx`\n* **Components**: `NotificationDropdown.tsx`, `AnnouncementWidget.tsx`\n* **Estimated Files**: 5 files\n* **Dependencies**: `socket.io-client`\n\n---\n\n### Module 12: Executive Dashboard & Analytics\n* **Tables**: Aggregated views over `employees`, `attendance_logs`, `payroll_slips`, `departments`.\n* **APIs**:\n  * `GET /api/v1/dashboard/metrics` - High-level headcounts, present today, pending leaves/expenses\n  * `GET /api/v1/dashboard/charts` - Department distribution & monthly payroll charts\n* **Controllers**: `dashboardController.ts`\n* **Services**: `dashboardService.ts`\n* **Repositories**: `dashboardRepository.ts`\n* **React Pages**: `DashboardPage.tsx`\n* **Components**: `MetricCard.tsx`, `DepartmentChart.tsx`, `PayrollBarChart.tsx`, `ActivityLog.tsx`\n* **Estimated Files**: 6 files\n* **Dependencies**: `recharts`, `lucide-react`\n\n---\n\n### Module 13: AI Executive Assistant\n* **Tables**: `ai_conversations`, `ai_queries`.\n* **APIs**:\n  * `GET /api/v1/ai/morning-brief` - Generate daily executive morning brief\n  * `POST /api/v1/ai/chat` - Natural language query over live HR metrics\n* **Controllers**: `aiController.ts`\n* **Services**: `aiService.ts`\n* **Repositories**: Leverages `dashboardRepository.ts` & `employeeRepository.ts`\n* **React Pages**: `WeeklyPlannerPage.tsx` (AI Assistant tab)\n* **Components**: `AiBriefBanner.tsx`, `AiChatWidget.tsx`\n* **Estimated Files**: 5 files\n* **Dependencies**: `@google/genai` (Gemini 3.6 Flash)\n\n---\n\n### Module 14: Mobile REST API & Gateway\n* **Tables**: `user_device_tokens`, `mobile_sessions`.\n* **APIs**:\n  * `POST /api/v1/mobile/auth/token-login` - Mobile fast authentication\n  * `POST /api/v1/mobile/attendance/quick-punch` - Compact payload GPS punch\n  * `GET /api/v1/mobile/me` - Profile overview for iOS/Android shell\n* **Controllers**: `mobileController.ts`\n* **Services**: Wraps `authService.ts` and `attendanceService.ts`\n* **Repositories**: Reuses existing core repositories\n* **React Pages**: N/A (Mobile Native / PWA Consumers)\n* **Components**: N/A\n* **Estimated Files**: 3 files\n* **Dependencies**: `firebase-admin`\n\n---\n\n### Module 15: Reports & Compliance Export Engine\n* **Tables**: Read-only aggregations across statutory tables (`pf_reports`, `esi_reports`, `tds_reports`).\n* **APIs**:\n  * `GET /api/v1/reports/attendance/csv` - Export attendance ledger CSV\n  * `GET /api/v1/reports/payroll/summary` - Statutory PF/ESI compliance breakdown\n* **Controllers**: `reportController.ts`\n* **Services**: `reportService.ts`\n* **Repositories**: `reportRepository.ts`\n* **React Pages**: `ReportsPage.tsx`\n* **Components**: `ReportFilterBar.tsx`, `ExportButton.tsx`\n* **Estimated Files**: 5 files\n* **Dependencies**: `json2csv`\n\n---\n\n## ARCHITECTURE SPECIFICATION SUMMARY\n\n* **Total Modules Specified**: 15 Enterprise Modules\n* **Total Estimated Architecture Files**: ~98 clean, single-responsibility files\n* **Core Technology Stack**: Node.js Express + Neon PostgreSQL (`pg`) + React 18 Vite + Gemini 3.6 Flash + Socket.io + Cloudinary\n* **Standard Response Envelope**: `{ \"success\": boolean, \"message\": string, \"data\": T }`\n* **Execution Status**: Architecture Blueprint complete and ready for execution."
