    thinking: "**Defining the Objective**\n\nI\'ve locked down the architecture blueprint, which is now the single source of truth. My primary focus is on the workflow. Right now, I\'m at the very beginning of the process. I\'m starting by defining the sprint objective. I need to make sure I am starting from a strong foundation.\n\n\n**Drafting the Proposal**\n\nI\'m now drafting the proposal for Sprint 1. I\'ve organized the document, and I\'m ready to follow the 7-step structure. It is focused on Core Architecture Alignment & Employees Module Hardening. I\'m waiting for your feedback before I proceed any further with coding.\n\n\n**Outlining the Sprint**\n\nI\'ve outlined Sprint 1. My focus is on the Employees Module and standardizing our shared infrastructure, particularly the Repository-Service-Controller layer. I\'m ensuring strict API response formatting and pure PostgreSQL persistence. I\'ve detailed the specific files created, including validators, middlewares, and services, as well as modifications to the employee repository.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "# Sprint 1 Proposal: Core Architecture Alignment & Employees Module\n\n## 1. Objective\nRefactor and harden the **Employees Module** into a production-grade 3-tier architecture (Repository \342\206\222 Service \342\206\222 Controller \342\206\222 Route) adhering strictly to the LOCKED Architecture Blueprint. Eliminate inline backend queries from controllers, isolate all frontend HTTP logic into client services, and enforce a standard global API response format `{ success, message, data }` backed by Neon PostgreSQL (`pg`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Files Created\n* **`src/backend/middlewares/responseHandler.ts`**: Standardized response helper enforcing `{ success, message, data }` formatting across all routes.\n* **`src/backend/validators/employeeValidator.ts`**: Express-validator / schema validator for employee payload validation (email format, required fields, role validation).\n* **`src/backend/services/employeeService.ts`**: Encapsulates business logic, salary calculation logic, employee code auto-generation, and permission checks.\n* **`src/services/employeeService.ts`**: Isolated frontend API service wrapping `apiClient` for employee CRUD and directory filters.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Files Modified\n* **`src/backend/repositories/employeeRepository.ts`**: Purged non-SQL logic; strictly executes PostgreSQL queries via `pool.query()`.\n* **`src/backend/controllers/employeeController.ts`**: Reduced to request validation and service invocation; utilizes standard response wrapper.\n* **`src/backend/routes/api.ts`**: Updated employee routes to include validation middlewares and refactored controller handlers.\n* **`src/pages/EmployeesPage.tsx`**: Updated to consume frontend `employeeService` instead of direct `fetch` calls.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Database Changes\n* **Database Engine**: Neon PostgreSQL (using `pg` pool, existing connection maintained).\n* **Table Verification**: `employees` table audit.\n* **Indexes Added**: Ensure performance indexes on `employees (tenant_id, is_deleted)`, `employees (email)`, and `employees (employee_code)`.\n* **No Schema Breaking Changes**.\n\n---\n\n## 5. API Endpoints\nAll endpoints will strictly return `{ success: boolean, message: string, data: T }`:\n\n| Method | Endpoint | Description | Auth Required |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **GET** | `/api/employees` | List all active/filtered employees | Yes (JWT) |\n| **GET** | `/api/employees/:id` | Get employee detailed profile | Yes (JWT) |\n| **POST** | `/api/employees` | Create new enterprise employee | Admin / HR |\n| **PUT** | `/api/employees/:id` | Update employee record | Admin / HR |\n| **DELETE** | `/api/employees/:id` | Soft delete employee (`is_deleted = true`) | Admin |\n| **PATCH** | `/api/employees/:id/restore` | Restore soft-deleted employee | Admin |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Testing Steps\n1. **API Schema Validation Test**: Execute `GET /api/employees` and verify response schema matches `{ success: true, message: string, data: [...] }`.\n2. **Employee Lifecycle Verification**:\n   * Create employee with duplicate email -> Verify 400 Validation Error response.\n   * Create employee with valid data -> Verify auto-generated `employee_code` and database insertion.\n   * Update salary & bank details -> Verify state persistence in Neon PostgreSQL.\n   * Soft-delete employee -> Verify employee excluded from active directory list.\n   * Restore employee -> Verify restoration to active directory.\n3. **Compilation & Quality Check**: Run `compile_applet` to confirm zero TypeScript compilation or bundle errors.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Rollback Plan\nIf any breaking issues arise during Sprint 1 execution:\n1. Revert changes to `src/backend/controllers/employeeController.ts`, `src/backend/repositories/employeeRepository.ts`, `src/backend/routes/api.ts`, and `src/pages/EmployeesPage.tsx` using file version state.\n2. Ensure core environment files (`server.ts`, `package.json`, `vite.config.ts`, `src/backend/database/db.ts`) remain completely untouched and active.\n\n---\n\n**Awaiting your approval to begin Sprint 1 implementation.**"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 451242538
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
