  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Confirming Initial Success**\n\nI\'ve got good news! The initial build completed successfully, and there were no errors reported. My next step involves meticulously cross-referencing the results against the sprint 1 checklist to guarantee alignment with all outlined verification requirements. I\'m focusing on ensuring all initial components like middlewares, the logger, the request validator, and rate limiting are properly set up.\n\n\n**Establishing Core Infrastructure**\n\nI\'ve been busy establishing the core infrastructure. I\'ve created the logger and validation utilities, alongside vital middlewares for handling errors, responses, request validation, and rate limiting. I\'ve also incorporated these into `server.ts`. I\342\200\231ve verified performance database indexes and I\'m ensuring everything is set up correctly, following the verification checks.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### Sprint 1: Project Foundation (Completed)\n\n#### 1. Objective\nEstablish the foundational infrastructure layers for **THEIAKSHI ONE Enterprise HRMS** \342\200\224 including enterprise logging, global error handling, request validation, rate limiting, and response formatting \342\200\224 without modifying the Employee module or business logic.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Files Created\n1. `src/backend/utils/logger.ts` \342\200\224 Structured enterprise logger (`INFO`, `WARN`, `ERROR`, `DEBUG`) with ISO timestamps and context metadata.\n2. `src/backend/middlewares/errorHandlerMiddleware.ts` \342\200\224 Global Express error-handling middleware that logs errors and returns standard `{ success: false, message, data: null }` responses.\n3. `src/backend/middlewares/responseHandler.ts` \342\200\224 Middleware extending Express `res` with helper methods (`res.success(...)`, `res.error(...)`).\n4. `src/backend/middlewares/validateRequest.ts` \342\200\224 Middleware executing reusable validation rule chains.\n5. `src/backend/middlewares/rateLimiterMiddleware.ts` \342\200\224 In-memory rate limiting middleware to protect endpoints against brute force and high concurrency bursts.\n6. `src/backend/validators/index.ts` \342\200\224 Reusable validation utilities (`isRequired`, `isEmail`, `isNumericId`, `isMinLength`).\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Files Modified & Reasons\n* **`server.ts`**: Registered `responseHandlerMiddleware`, `rateLimiterMiddleware`, and `errorHandlerMiddleware` into the Express application pipeline to activate global error catching and request rate protection.\n\n> **Note**: `employeeRepository.ts`, `employeeController.ts`, `employeeService.ts`, and `EmployeesPage.tsx` were left completely untouched as instructed.\n\n---\n\n#### 4. Architecture Verification Summary\n* **Database Indexes**: Verified index definitions in `schema.ts` (`idx_emp_code`, `idx_emp_email`, `idx_emp_dept`, `idx_emp_branch`, `idx_att_emp_date`, `idx_leave_emp`, `idx_payroll_emp_year_month`, `idx_tasks_proj`, `idx_notif_emp`).\n* **PostgreSQL Engine**: Verified single database connection manager (`dbService` in `src/backend/database/db.ts`).\n* **JWT Flow**: Verified token issuance and verification in `jwt.ts` and `authMiddleware.ts`.\n* **Route Registration**: Verified `/api/v1` route mounting in `server.ts` and `api.ts`.\n\n---\n\n#### 5. Testing Steps\n1. Executed full application build (`compile_applet`) \342\200\224 **Build Succeeded** with zero compilation errors.\n2. Verified backend health check route `/api/health`.\n3. Verified error response formats and logger output stream.\n\n---\n\n#### 6. Rollback Plan\nIf needed, remove the three middleware imports from `server.ts` and delete the six newly created files in `src/backend/middlewares`, `src/backend/utils`, and `src/backend/validators`.\n\n---\n\n### Awaiting Approval\nSprint 1 foundation is complete and compiled successfully. Please provide approval to begin **Sprint 2: Employees Module Refactoring**."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 430121983
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
