  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Sprint Scope**\n\nI\'ve got the green light on Sprint 1! Architecture\'s locked, and I\'m specifically instructed to avoid changes to critical files like `server.ts`, `package.json`, `vite.config.ts`, `tsconfig.json`, database connection, authentication, and Sprint 1 middleware unless a compilation error pops up. Seems like the scope is pretty tightly defined now.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "# Sprint 2 Plan: Employees Module\n\nSprint 1 (Project Foundation) has been locked and accepted. We are ready to propose **Sprint 2: Employees Module**.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Objective\nTransform the Employee management capabilities into a production-ready enterprise module with full CRUD operations, department & designation linking, compensation profiles, and strict database query isolation.\n\n### 2. Proposed Files to Create / Refactor\n#### Backend:\n* **Create:** `src/backend/services/employeeService.ts` (Isolated business logic, validation, employee code generation, CTC calculations).\n* **Modify:** `src/backend/repositories/employeeRepository.ts` (Clean SQL queries for employee search, profile retrieval, updates, and creation).\n* **Modify:** `src/backend/controllers/employeeController.ts` (HTTP request validation, standard response format `{ success, message, data }`).\n\n#### Frontend:\n* **Create:** `src/services/employeeService.ts` (Client API integration using standard HTTP requests).\n* **Modify:** `src/pages/EmployeesPage.tsx` (Refactored UI with responsive cards/table, department filter, search bar, employee creation modal, and view drawer).\n* **Create:** `src/components/employees/EmployeeModal.tsx` (Extracted modal component for adding/editing employees to adhere to the <300 line file rule).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Database Changes\n* No schema migration required; existing `employees`, `departments`, and `designations` tables in PostgreSQL will be fully utilized.\n* Verification of existing foreign keys and `employee_code` UNIQUE constraint.\n\n---\n\n### 4. API Endpoints\n* `GET /api/v1/employees` - List all employees with department & designation join\n* `GET /api/v1/employees/:id` - Get detailed profile of a single employee\n* `POST /api/v1/employees` - Create a new employee with generated `employee_code`\n* `PUT /api/v1/employees/:id` - Update employee details & job status\n* `DELETE /api/v1/employees/:id` - Soft-delete or terminate employee record\n\n---\n\n### 5. Testing Steps\n1. Verify `GET /api/v1/employees` returns normalized JSON `{ success: true, message: \"...\", data: [...] }`.\n2. Test creating a new employee via the UI modal and verify instant entry in PostgreSQL.\n3. Test searching employees by name, department, or employee code in real-time.\n4. Verify non-breaking behavior across authentication & sidebar navigation.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Rollback Plan\nIf any compile or execution error occurs, git changes for Sprint 2 files can be reverted cleanly without affecting Sprint 1 foundation middleware or global server configuration.\n\n---\n\n**Please review and approve this plan to begin Sprint 2 execution.**"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 155430175
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
