  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Sprint 2 Prompt**\n\nI\'ve carefully reread the Sprint 2 prompt and am now starting to break down the required deliverables. Specifically, I\'m focusing on identifying all the files that need to be created as part of this sprint.\n\n\n**Listing File Updates**\n\nI\'ve made significant progress by outlining the key file updates needed. I\'m focusing on `employeeService.ts` in both backend and frontend, separating business logic from API calls. I am also planning to connect the routes to the backend via `employeeController.ts` . Finally, I\'ll update the frontend UI and have finalized changes to `EmployeesPage.tsx`.\n\n\n**Defining API Endpoint Behavior**\n\nI\'m now detailing the behavior of each API endpoint. I\'ve worked to define data validation and error handling for employee creation and updates, specifically focusing on unique identifiers and sensitive data. I\'m also planning the logic for auto-generating the employee code, and incorporating hashing for security. I\'m thinking about pagination, search filters, and sorting parameters for employee lists, aiming for robust functionality.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### Sprint 2 Proposal: Employees Module Implementation\n\nHere is the implementation plan for **Sprint 2 \342\200\223 Employees Module**. No code will be written until you approve this proposal.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Files Created\n* **`src/backend/services/employeeService.ts`**\n  * *Purpose*: Server-side business logic for employee operations, including auto-generating employee codes (e.g., `EMP-1002`), checking duplicate emails/codes, salary & role validation, soft delete, and restore logic.\n* **`src/services/employeeService.ts`**\n  * *Purpose*: Frontend API client service for all employee operations (`getEmployees`, `getEmployeeById`, `createEmployee`, `updateEmployee`, `deleteEmployee`, `restoreEmployee`). Guarantees no direct `fetch` calls in React pages.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Files Modified\n* **`src/backend/controllers/employeeController.ts`**\n  * *Purpose*: Refactored to delegate business rules to the backend `employeeService`, leverage the request validation middleware from Sprint 1, and return standardized `{ success, message, data }` responses.\n* **`src/backend/routes/api.ts`**\n  * *Purpose*: Mounts employee endpoints with authentication (`authMiddleware`), request validation (`validateRequest`), and parameters binding (`isNumericId`, etc.).\n* **`src/pages/EmployeesPage.tsx`**\n  * *Purpose*: Refactored to consume the frontend `employeeService`. Adds support for server-side pagination, live search, department/role/status filters, employee detail modal (bank details, emergency contacts, salary structure, manager assignment), and soft-delete/restore toggle.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Database Changes\n* **No table structure changes needed**: The existing Neon PostgreSQL schema (`src/backend/database/schema.ts`) already defines the full `employees` table with all necessary fields (`employee_code`, `email`, `salary`, `bank_account`, `ifsc_code`, `pan_number`, `aadhaar_number`, `emergency_contact_name`, `emergency_contact_phone`, `reporting_manager_id`, `is_deleted`, etc.).\n* **Index verification**: Ensure SQL indexes exist on `employees(email)`, `employees(employee_code)`, `employees(department_id)`, and `employees(is_deleted)`.\n\n---\n\n### 4. API Endpoints\n* `GET /api/v1/employees` \342\200\223 Paginated list with search, department, role, status, sorting, and includeDeleted parameters.\n* `GET /api/v1/employees/:id` \342\200\223 Fetch detailed profile of a single employee.\n* `POST /api/v1/employees` \342\200\223 Register a new employee with auto-generated code, password hashing, and duplicate checks.\n* `PUT /api/v1/employees/:id` \342\200\223 Update employee info (roles, salary, bank details, manager assignment, emergency contacts).\n* `DELETE /api/v1/employees/:id` \342\200\223 Soft delete employee (`is_deleted = true`, `status = \'INACTIVE\'`).\n* `PATCH /api/v1/employees/:id/restore` \342\200\223 Restore soft-deleted employee (`is_deleted = false`, `status = \'ACTIVE\'`).\n\n---\n\n### 5. Why Each File is Changing\n1. **`src/backend/services/employeeService.ts`**: Implements pure business logic separation between the database queries (Repository) and HTTP controllers (Controller).\n2. **`src/services/employeeService.ts`**: Encapsulates API calls cleanly so components only deal with state and UI rendering.\n3. **`src/backend/controllers/employeeController.ts`**: Removes direct database calls from the controller layer and enforces the standard response structure.\n4. **`src/backend/routes/api.ts`**: Registers missing endpoints (e.g., `restoreEmployee`) and attaches Sprint 1 validation rules.\n5. **`src/pages/EmployeesPage.tsx`**: Provides an enterprise-grade UI experience with complete pagination, filtering, soft-delete management, and full profile editing.\n\n---\n\n**Awaiting your approval to begin Sprint 2 execution.**"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 666954625
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
