  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Sprint 3 Goals**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the scope for Sprint 3, focusing specifically on the Attendance Module. I\'ve outlined the core features we need to implement: employee punch in/out, managing breaks, calculating work duration, and tracking late arrivals, early exits, and overtime. We also need to implement attendance history and daily attendance views.\n\n\n**Planning Monthly Attendance**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of monthly attendance. I\'ve broken it down into an Attendance Calendar, Dashboard, and am integrating GPS coordinates and office geofence. Also, Shift Timings and Attendance Status are in scope. I\'ve confirmed that the frontend service `src/services/attendanceService.ts` needs to be created, and the backend needs an updated `attendanceRepository.ts` for these new features.\n\n\n**Implementing Attendance Logic**\n\nI\'m deep in the implementation. I\'ve added the crucial business logic for breaks, shift timings, overtime, geofence validation with GPS, and also created the monthly attendance summary. I\'ve also added corresponding handlers in the backend and registered appropriate endpoints. The UI is being updated to reflect the new functionality, with live clock, geolocation status, and interactive action cards.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### SPRINT 3 \342\200\223 ATTENDANCE MODULE PROPOSAL\n\n#### 1. Files Created\n1. `src/services/attendanceService.ts`\n   - Dedicated frontend HTTP client for all Attendance API interactions (Punch In, Punch Out, Break Start, Break End, Today Status, History, Monthly Calendar).\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Files Modified\n1. `src/backend/repositories/attendanceRepository.ts`\n   - Added repository methods for break tracking (`breakStart`, `breakEnd`), monthly attendance queries, work duration updates, and overtime calculations using parameterized SQL.\n2. `src/backend/services/attendanceService.ts`\n   - Added business logic for break duration management, shift timing verification (late arrival, early exit threshold), overtime calculation (>8 hours/day or shift duration), geofence distance calculation using Haversine formula, and monthly calendar summary generation.\n3. `src/backend/controllers/attendanceController.ts`\n   - Added request handlers for `breakStart`, `breakEnd`, and `getMonthlyAttendance`.\n4. `src/backend/routes/api.ts`\n   - Registered endpoints: `POST /attendance/break-start`, `POST /attendance/break-end`, and `GET /attendance/monthly`.\n5. `src/pages/AttendancePage.tsx`\n   - Updated UI to consume `attendanceService`:\n     - Live Clock & Live Work Duration Timer\n     - Geofence GPS status indicator\n     - Punch In / Punch Out / Break Start / Break End interactive buttons\n     - Monthly Attendance Calendar & Monthly Attendance History Stream\n     - Attendance Statistics Dashboard (Total Hours, Overtime, Late Count, Break Time)\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Database Changes\nNo schema migrations needed. Utilizing existing Neon PostgreSQL `attendance` table:\n- Columns used: `id`, `employee_id`, `date`, `punch_in`, `punch_out`, `punch_in_lat`, `punch_in_lng`, `punch_out_lat`, `punch_out_lng`, `break_start`, `break_end`, `work_hours`, `break_hours`, `status`, `is_late`, `is_early_exit`, `is_overtime`, `shift_name`.\n\n---\n\n#### 4. API Endpoints\n- `POST /api/v1/attendance/punch-in` \342\200\224 Punch in with GPS coordinates and geofence check.\n- `POST /api/v1/attendance/punch-out` \342\200\224 Punch out with total work hours calculation.\n- `POST /api/v1/attendance/break-start` \342\200\224 Start employee break.\n- `POST /api/v1/attendance/break-end` \342\200\224 End employee break and update cumulative break time.\n- `GET /api/v1/attendance/status` \342\200\224 Get today\'s punch and break status for current employee.\n- `GET /api/v1/attendance/history` \342\200\224 Get personal attendance history.\n- `GET /api/v1/attendance/monthly` \342\200\224 Get monthly attendance summary & calendar data.\n- `GET /api/v1/attendance/today` \342\200\224 Get today\'s attendance stream for all employees (HR/Manager view).\n\n---\n\n#### 5. Testing Plan\n1. **Punch In Test**: Trigger `POST /attendance/punch-in` with GPS coordinates. Verify late check and status assignment (`PRESENT` / `LATE`).\n2. **Break Cycle Test**: Trigger `POST /attendance/break-start` and `POST /attendance/break-end`. Verify break duration calculation.\n3. **Punch Out Test**: Trigger `POST /attendance/punch-out`. Verify total work hours, overtime calculation, and shift completion status.\n4. **Monthly Calendar Test**: Fetch `GET /attendance/monthly` for current month and verify accurate aggregate statistics.\n5. **Frontend Flow Test**: Verify `AttendancePage.tsx` updates in real-time on punch/break actions via `src/services/attendanceService.ts`.\n\n---\n\nWaiting for approval to proceed with Sprint 3 implementation."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 336801160
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
