  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Awaiting Code Change Approval**\n\nI\'m currently paused on code modifications, as the user has requested that I wait for final approval before implementing the suggested enterprise features. I\'m ready to move forward as soon as I get the green light.\n\n\n**Clarifying Sprint 3 Planning**\n\nI\'ve re-read the user\'s instructions and confirmed I need to create a Sprint 3 proposal *first*. This proposal will encompass the new enterprise features and address all workflow requirements, specifically objective, files created/modified, DB changes, API endpoints, testing, and rollback. I\'ll await approval of this design before any code implementation.\n\n\n**Detailing Sprint 3 Proposal**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the Sprint 3 proposal, meticulously outlining all required details. I\'ve started fleshing out the \'Objective\' section, defining the comprehensive scope of the Enterprise Attendance Module. This includes specific functionalities like punch-in/out, geofencing, shift management, various attendance statuses, and a real-time dashboard with analytics. I\'ll continue to fill out the remaining sections to create a complete and approved Sprint 3 proposal.\n\n\n**Outlining API Integration**\n\nI\'m now detailing the API integration for the Enterprise Attendance Module. Specifically, I\'m defining the Manager Live Dashboard API (`GET /api/v1/attendance/live`). This will integrate with the existing Neon PostgreSQL database. I\'m also planning the new files and existing file modifications, with specific attention to the `attendanceRepository.ts`, `attendanceService.ts`, and `attendanceController.ts` files, to ensure comprehensive functionality. I\'m working on the routes and frontend integration next.\n\n\n**Defining API Requirements**\n\nI\'m presently working on detailing the API endpoints. I have finalized the routes: `POST /api/v1/attendance/punch-in`, `POST /api/v1/attendance/punch-out`, `POST /api/v1/attendance/break-start`, `POST /api/v1/attendance/break-end`, and `GET /api/v1/attendance/my-status`. I\'m integrating GPS coordinates and work summaries. No new database tables are needed, just parameterized SQL queries. I will also be creating the UI for the live working timer, interactive punch buttons, and manager view.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### SPRINT 3 \342\200\223 ENTERPRISE ATTENDANCE MODULE PLAN\n\n#### 1. Objective\nImplement a production-grade Enterprise Attendance Module adhering strictly to the clean architecture (`Routes -> Controller -> Service -> Repository -> PostgreSQL`):\n- **Core Punch Flow**: Punch In, Punch Out, Break Start, Break End with real-time duration tracking.\n- **Enterprise Statuses**: `PRESENT`, `LATE`, `HALF_DAY`, `ABSENT`, `ON_LEAVE`, `HOLIDAY`, `WEEK_OFF`, `REMOTE`, `WORK_FROM_HOME`, `FIELD_VISIT`.\n- **Shift Management Integration**: Calculate Late Arrival, Early Exit, and Overtime based on employee assigned shifts (`General`, `Morning`, `Evening`, `Night`, `Flexible`).\n- **Multi-Location Geofencing**: Calculate Haversine GPS distance against branch location coordinates and return `distance`, `insideGeofence`, and `allowed`.\n- **Live Employee Dashboard**: Real-time counter for Current Working Time, Current Break Time, and Remaining Shift Time.\n- **Attendance Analytics**: Average Login, Average Logout, Average Hours, Late Count, Overtime Count, and Attendance %.\n- **Manager Live Dashboard API**: `GET /api/v1/attendance/live` returning active live state of all organizational employees.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Files Created\n- `src/services/attendanceService.ts` \342\200\224 Frontend API client wrapper for attendance operations.\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Files Modified\n- `src/backend/repositories/attendanceRepository.ts` \342\200\224 Enhanced parameterized SQL queries for multi-status logs, date ranges, live status queries, and analytics aggregation.\n- `src/backend/services/attendanceService.ts` \342\200\224 Business logic for shift rules, geofence distance calculation, status classification, break durations, and live manager status compilation.\n- `src/backend/controllers/attendanceController.ts` \342\200\224 Controllers for punch actions, status retrieval, live manager views, and analytics.\n- `src/backend/routes/api.ts` \342\200\224 Route registration for `/attendance/live`, `/attendance/analytics`, and punch handlers.\n- `src/pages/AttendancePage.tsx` \342\200\224 Full UI implementation with live counters, GPS geofence checker, monthly calendar, analytics cards, and live manager monitoring.\n\n---\n\n#### 4. Database Changes\n- **No DDL schema modifications required**. Uses existing PostgreSQL tables (`attendance_logs`, `employees`, `branches`, `shifts`).\n- All queries utilize parameterized SQL joining branches and shifts for exact coordinate evaluation and shift rules.\n\n---\n\n#### 5. API Endpoints\n- `POST /api/v1/attendance/punch-in` \342\200\224 Register punch in with GPS coordinates (`latitude`, `longitude`, `workMode`).\n- `POST /api/v1/attendance/punch-out` \342\200\224 Register punch out and calculate final work hours and overtime.\n- `POST /api/v1/attendance/break-start` \342\200\224 Pause shift for break.\n- `POST /api/v1/attendance/break-end` \342\200\224 Resume shift from break.\n- `GET /api/v1/attendance/my-status` \342\200\224 Get today\'s attendance log, active status, and shift counters.\n- `GET /api/v1/attendance/logs` \342\200\224 Query historical attendance logs with status, date, and pagination filters.\n- `GET /api/v1/attendance/live` \342\200\224 Manager endpoint for active workforce live status.\n- `GET /api/v1/attendance/analytics` \342\200\224 Aggregated attendance metrics and performance stats.\n\n---\n\n#### 6. Testing Steps\n1. **Geofence Check**: Test Punch In with coordinates inside and outside allowed branch radius. Confirm `distance` and `insideGeofence` values.\n2. **Shift Timings**: Verify Punch In after shift start time marks status as `LATE`.\n3. **Break & Work Counters**: Verify live break duration and total work duration calculation upon Punch Out.\n4. **Manager Live API**: Execute `GET /api/v1/attendance/live` to verify real-time status feed.\n5. **Frontend UI**: Test live timers, monthly calendar rendering, and history filters.\n\n---\n\n#### 7. Rollback Plan\n- Revert modified attendance backend files (`attendanceRepository.ts`, `attendanceService.ts`, `attendanceController.ts`, `api.ts`) and frontend files (`AttendancePage.tsx`, `src/services/attendanceService.ts`). Sprint 1 and Sprint 2 modules will remain untouched.\n\n---\n\n**Awaiting your approval to execute Sprint 3.**"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 123619859
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
