    thinking: "**Analyzing Prompt Requirements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specific constraints for Sprint 4. The instructions are clear; previous sprints are off-limits. My focus is entirely on the structure, specifically the \"Routes\" architecture. I need to determine the implications of this architectural choice and how it will influence development.\n\n\n**Defining Leave Implementation**\n\nI\'ve moved on to defining the leave types, workflow, and features required. I\'m carefully considering the business rules to ensure accuracy. The design includes both employee and manager dashboards for ease of access to necessary information. I\'m focusing on leave application and the approval processes.\n\n\n**Formulating Technical Plan**\n\nI\'m structuring the technical plan for the frontend leave service. The design now includes specific file creations: `leaveService.ts` for the frontend API layer, eliminating direct axios/fetch in components. Additionally, I\'ve defined a `leaveRepository.ts` file in the backend to enhance existing leave functionality. I\'m carefully detailing the database changes, API endpoints, testing plan, and rollback plan for approval.\n\n\n**Detailing New Implementations**\n\nI\'m now implementing the new technical designs. I\'m focusing on the backend and frontend changes required for the leave service. This includes a robust business logic layer (`leaveService.ts`), a controller layer (`leaveController.ts`), and a refactored UI (`LeavePage.tsx`) for a complete enterprise leave solution. API routes have been added to `/src/backend/routes/api.ts`, and the schema has been extended. Finally, I\'m integrating enhanced leave types and database schema updates, including support for draft leave states.\n\n\n**Defining Data Schemas**\n\nI\'m now detailing the database schemas. I have the leave request states defined: `SUBMITTED`, `MANAGER_PENDING`, `HR_PENDING`, `APPROVED`, `REJECTED`, and `CANCELLED`. I\'m also adding `is_half_day`, `half_day_type`, `is_hourly`, `hours_requested`, `attachment_url`, `manager_comments`, `hr_comments`, `manager_approved_by`, and `hr_approved_by` to the schema. In addition, I\'m integrating a `holidays` table with fields such as `id`, `title`, `date`, `is_optional`, and `description`.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Here is the technical architectural proposal for **Sprint 4 \342\200\223 Enterprise Leave Management**.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Files Created\n1. **`/src/services/leaveService.ts`** *(Frontend API Service)*\n   - Encapsulates all leave-related HTTP operations (`getMyLeaves`, `applyLeave`, `cancelLeave`, `processApproval`, `bulkApprove`, `getCalendar`, `getHolidays`).\n   - Ensures **zero direct `fetch` or `axios` calls** inside React UI components.\n\n2. **`/src/backend/controllers/leaveController.ts`** *(Backend Controller)*\n   - Segregates leave logic from `attendanceController.ts` into a dedicated controller following the strict `Routes -> Controller -> Service -> Repository -> PostgreSQL` architecture.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Files Modified\n1. **`/src/backend/repositories/leaveRepository.ts`**\n   - Contains all SQL queries for multi-tier workflows, overlap conflict checks, holiday queries, balance deduction/restoration transactions, and bulk approval queries.\n2. **`/src/backend/services/leaveService.ts`**\n   - Encapsulates business validation: past date validation, balance checks, leave collision detection, holiday clash checks, self-approval restriction, and stage transitions (`Draft` \342\206\222 `Submitted` \342\206\222 `Manager Approval` \342\206\222 `HR Approval` \342\206\222 `Approved` / `Rejected` / `Cancelled`).\n3. **`/src/backend/routes/api.ts`**\n   - Registers new RESTful API endpoints for Enterprise Leave Management.\n4. **`/src/backend/database/schema.ts`**\n   - Adds Drizzle / SQL schema definitions for the `holidays` table and extends the `leaves` table with half-day/hourly fields, attachments, and multi-tier approval metadata.\n5. **`/src/pages/LeavePage.tsx`**\n   - Refactored Enterprise Leave Dashboard featuring Leave Balances, Application Form (with attachment support & half-day selectors), Manager & HR Approval Panels, Team Leave Calendar, and Holiday Calendar.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Database Changes\n\n#### Existing `leave_types` Table Seeding / Updates\nSupport 9 standard enterprise leave types:\n- `CASUAL` (Casual Leave)\n- `SICK` (Sick Leave)\n- `PRIVILEGE` (Privilege / Earned Leave)\n- `MATERNITY` (Maternity Leave)\n- `PATERNITY` (Paternity Leave)\n- `BEREAVEMENT` (Bereavement Leave)\n- `COMPENSATORY_OFF` (Compensatory Off)\n- `OPTIONAL_HOLIDAY` (Optional Holiday)\n- `WFH` (Work From Home Request)\n\n#### Table Extensions on `leaves`:\n```sql\nALTER TABLE leaves ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS status VARCHAR(30) DEFAULT \'SUBMITTED\';\n-- Allowed status values: DRAFT, SUBMITTED, MANAGER_PENDING, HR_PENDING, APPROVED, REJECTED, CANCELLED\n\nALTER TABLE leaves ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS is_half_day BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE;\nALTER TABLE leaves ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS half_day_type VARCHAR(20); -- FIRST_HALF, SECOND_HALF\nALTER TABLE leaves ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS is_hourly BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE;\nALTER TABLE leaves ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS hours_requested NUMERIC(4,2) DEFAULT 0.00;\nALTER TABLE leaves ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS attachment_url TEXT;\nALTER TABLE leaves ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS manager_comments TEXT;\nALTER TABLE leaves ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS hr_comments TEXT;\nALTER TABLE leaves ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS manager_approved_by INTEGER REFERENCES employees(id);\nALTER TABLE leaves ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS hr_approved_by INTEGER REFERENCES employees(id);\n```\n\n#### New `holidays` Table:\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS holidays (\n  id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,\n  title VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,\n  date DATE NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  is_optional BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE,\n  description TEXT,\n  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n);\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. API Endpoints\n\n| Method | Endpoint | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `GET` | `/api/v1/leaves` | List employee or team leave applications |\n| `POST` | `/api/v1/leaves` | Create or submit a new leave request |\n| `GET` | `/api/v1/leaves/balances` | Get current leave entitlement balances |\n| `GET` | `/api/v1/leaves/types` | Retrieve active leave types |\n| `GET` | `/api/v1/leaves/calendar` | Team & department leave calendar view |\n| `GET` | `/api/v1/leaves/holidays` | Company holiday calendar |\n| `PUT` | `/api/v1/leaves/:id` | Update draft/pending leave request |\n| `POST` | `/api/v1/leaves/:id/cancel` | Cancel leave request & restore balance |\n| `POST` | `/api/v1/leaves/:id/approve` | Process approval (Manager / HR) |\n| `POST` | `/api/v1/leaves/:id/reject` | Reject leave request with comments |\n| `POST` | `/api/v1/leaves/bulk-approve` | Bulk approve multiple pending requests |\n\n---\n\n### 5. Business Rules Enforcement\n1. **Past Date Check**: `start_date` cannot be earlier than today\'s date for standard leaves.\n2. **Balance Validation**: Requested days/hours cannot exceed available `remaining` balance for the selected leave type.\n3. **Conflict Detection**: Queries database to ensure no overlapping active or approved leave exists for the same employee.\n4. **Holiday Conflict Validation**: Prevents applying for leave on official company holidays.\n5. **Self-Approval Guard**: Manager ID in approval payload cannot match `employee_id`.\n6. **Automatic Deduction & Restoration**:\n   - Deducts from `leave_balances.remaining` and increments `used` upon final approval.\n   - Restores balance (`remaining += total_days`, `used -= total_days`) if an approved leave is cancelled.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Testing Plan\n- [ ] **Apply Leave**: Verify creation of full-day, multi-day, half-day, and WFH requests.\n- [ ] **Validation Checks**: Confirm rejection when applying for past dates, exceeding balance, or overlapping dates.\n- [ ] **Workflow Steps**: Test transitions: `Draft` \342\206\222 `Submitted` \342\206\222 `Manager Approval` \342\206\222 `HR Approval` \342\206\222 `Approved`.\n- [ ] **Cancellation & Restoration**: Cancel an approved leave and verify `leave_balances` restoration.\n- [ ] **Bulk Approval**: Test selecting multiple pending requests and approving in a single transaction.\n- [ ] **Calendar Views**: Verify team leave entries and upcoming company holidays render accurately.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Rollback Plan\n- If any issues arise during execution, all changes are isolated to the `Leave` domain files (`leaveRepository.ts`, `leaveService.ts`, `leaveController.ts`, `LeavePage.tsx`, `/src/services/leaveService.ts`).\n- Core modules (Sprint 1, Sprint 2 Employees, Sprint 3 Attendance, Database connection, Auth, Server.ts) remain completely untouched and unlocked.\n\n---\n\n**Awaiting your approval to begin implementation of Sprint 4.**"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 965510927
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
