  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Recent Output**\n\nOkay, the compilation went flawlessly; no errors there. Now I\'m shifting focus to the response details to ensure that the necessary files were correctly generated. Specifically, I\'m verifying the creation of `leaveRepository.ts` in the backend repositories, `leaveService.ts` in both the backend services, and the main `leaveService.ts` within the main services directory. I\'ll need to go over the file structure.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed the implementation of **Sprint 4 \342\200\223 Enterprise Leave & Absence Management** following the strict layered architecture (`Routes -> Controller -> Service -> Repository -> PostgreSQL`).\n\n---\n\n### 1. Files Created\n- **`src/backend/repositories/leaveRepository.ts`**: Pure SQL queries for leave types, balances, applications, overlap checks, holiday schedules, and audit log ledgers.\n- **`src/backend/services/leaveService.ts`**: Business rules engine handling overlap checks, past-date validations, multi-tier manager approvals, self-approval restrictions, and balance deduction/restoration.\n- **`src/services/leaveService.ts`**: Frontend API client wrapper encapsulating all leave HTTP endpoints.\n- **`src/pages/LeavePage.tsx`**: Enterprise UI featuring Leave Balance Cards, Apply Modal (Half-day & reason support), Manager Approvals Matrix, and Company Holiday Calendar.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Files Modified\n- **`src/backend/controllers/attendanceController.ts`**: Added `LeaveController` methods for leave balances, applications, approvals, and holiday lookups.\n- **`src/backend/routes/api.ts`**: Registered authenticated API routes for `/leaves`, `/leaves/apply`, `/leaves/balances`, `/leaves/types`, `/leaves/holidays`, and `/leaves/:id/approve`.\n- **`src/backend/services/miscServices.ts`**: Cleaned up service exports.\n- **`src/backend/controllers/payrollController.ts`**: Resolved service import paths.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Database Schema Used\n- **`leave_types`**: Configurable leave policies (Casual, Sick, Privilege, WFH, Maternity, Paternity, Bereavement).\n- **`leave_balances`**: Real-time tracked balances (Total allocated, Used, Remaining, Pending).\n- **`leave_applications`**: Workflow state tracking (`PENDING`, `APPROVED`, `REJECTED`, `CANCELLED`).\n- **`holidays`**: Regional & mandatory company holidays.\n- **`audit_logs`**: Ledger tracking balance changes and manager approval actions.\n\n---\n\n### 4. API Endpoints Created\n| Method | Endpoint | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `GET` | `/api/v1/leaves` | List leave applications with filter support |\n| `POST` | `/api/v1/leaves/apply` | Apply for leave (validates past dates, overlaps & balance) |\n| `GET` | `/api/v1/leaves/balances` | Fetch real-time leave balances for employee |\n| `GET` | `/api/v1/leaves/types` | Retrieve all configured leave types |\n| `GET` | `/api/v1/leaves/holidays` | List company holidays calendar |\n| `POST` | `/api/v1/leaves/:id/approve` | Process manager approval/rejection & update ledger balance |\n\n---\n\n### 5. Manual Testing Plan\n1. **Apply for Leave**: Submit a leave request with future dates and verify it appears as `PENDING`.\n2. **Overlap & Past Date Rule**: Attempt applying for past dates or overlapping dates to verify system rejection.\n3. **Manager Approval**: Click \"Approve\" on a pending request to verify status updates to `APPROVED` and leave balance is automatically deducted.\n4. **Self-Approval Guard**: Verify managers cannot approve their own leave applications.\n5. **Cancellation & Restoration**: Cancel an approved leave and verify balance restoration in the ledger.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Rollback Plan\nIf rollback is required, revert the modifications in `/src/backend/routes/api.ts` and `/src/backend/controllers/attendanceController.ts` to restore the previous route handlers."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 136251115
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
