  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Implementation Verification**\n\nI\'m currently focused on structuring the implementation verification report for Sprint 4\'s Leave Management feature, specifically addressing the 5 key questions. My primary task is to ensure the report accurately reflects the code\'s behavior without making any code modifications. I\'m taking care to format my responses to answer each question comprehensively.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "# Sprint 4 \342\200\223 Enterprise Leave Management Verification Report\n\n---\n\n### 1. Leave Endpoints Placement\n**Question:** Why were Leave endpoints implemented inside `attendanceController.ts` instead of `leaveController.ts`?  \n**Explanation:**  \nDuring initial consolidation, `LeaveController` was declared inside `src/backend/controllers/attendanceController.ts` alongside `AttendanceController` to streamline route handlers. However, to strictly honor the **Routes \342\206\222 Controller \342\206\222 Service \342\206\222 Repository \342\206\222 PostgreSQL** modular separation architecture, `LeaveController` will be isolated into its own dedicated `leaveController.ts` file upon approval.\n\n---\n\n### 2. File Status: `leaveController.ts`\n**Question:** Does `leaveController.ts` exist?  \n**Status:** **No** (It was previously defined inside `attendanceController.ts`).  \n**Action Plan:** `src/backend/controllers/leaveController.ts` will be created as an independent file, and all leave endpoints in `src/backend/routes/api.ts` will reference this dedicated controller.\n\n---\n\n### 3. API Completeness Analysis\n\n| Endpoint | Status | Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `GET /api/v1/leaves` | **Implemented** | Retrieves team & employee leave applications |\n| `POST /api/v1/leaves/apply` | **Implemented** | Submits new leave application |\n| `GET /api/v1/leaves/balances` | **Implemented** | Fetches active leave balances |\n| `GET /api/v1/leaves/types` | **Implemented** | Lists all configurable leave categories |\n| `GET /api/v1/leaves/holidays` | **Implemented** | Returns mandatory and optional holiday schedules |\n| `POST /api/v1/leaves/:id/approve` | **Implemented** | Processes approval, rejection, and balance deductions |\n| `PUT /api/v1/leaves/:id` | **Pending** | Editable drafts before manager review |\n| `POST /api/v1/leaves/:id/cancel` | **Pending** | Dedicated cancellation route (currently handled via approval status `CANCELLED`) |\n| `POST /api/v1/leaves/bulk-approve` | **Pending** | Batch approval endpoint for managers |\n| `GET /api/v1/leaves/calendar` | **Pending** | Team calendar view endpoint |\n\n---\n\n### 4. Workflow Transition Alignment\n**Question:** Alignment between planned multi-tier workflow (`Draft` \342\206\222 `Submitted` \342\206\222 `Manager Approval` \342\206\222 `HR Approval` \342\206\222 `Approved`) vs actual (`PENDING` \342\206\222 `APPROVED` / `REJECTED` / `CANCELLED`).  \n**Explanation:**  \nThe initial build implemented a unified state machine (`PENDING`, `APPROVED`, `REJECTED`, `CANCELLED`). In the full implementation plan:\n- **`DRAFT`**: Saved locally/DB prior to submission.\n- **`SUBMITTED` / `PENDING_MANAGER`**: Initial status upon applying.\n- **`PENDING_HR`**: Triggered after Manager approval if HR clearance is required for multi-day or special leave types.\n- **`APPROVED`**: Final approved state that executes automated balance deductions in `leave_balances`.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Enterprise Feature Matrix Status\n\n| Feature | Status | Details |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Leave Policy Engine** | **Implemented** | Dynamic leave types (`leave_types` table with min/max days, notice periods, and colors). |\n| **Leave Ledger** | **Implemented** | Changes recorded with audit trail logs in `audit_logs` table (`LEAVE_LEDGER`). |\n| **Regional / Company Holidays**| **Implemented** | Configurable via `holidays` database table and exposed via `/leaves/holidays`. |\n| **Attachment Support** | **Implemented** | DB column `attachment_url` and payload parameter supported in API and UI. |\n| **Carry Forward** | **Pending** | Requires cron/scheduled script to rollover unused balances at year-end. |\n| **Monthly Accrual** | **Pending** | Requires cron/service to add monthly pro-rated credits (+1.5 days/month). |\n| **Sandwich Rule** | **Pending** | Calculation logic to flag weekend/holiday sandwiching across leave dates. |\n\n---\n\n### Summary & Next Steps\nNo code changes were performed during this verification turn. Awaiting instructions to create `leaveController.ts` and add the remaining endpoints and features."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 899969412
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
