  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Sprint Completion**\n\nI\'m focusing on SPRINT 4.1\'s completion. Task 1 saw the creation of `/src/backend/controllers/leaveController.ts`, successfully moving leave endpoints. Task 2, the implementation of leave creation, modification, and deletion endpoints within the new controller, is now fully tested and functioning. I am currently working on Task 3, which is the comprehensive documentation phase.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "# Sprint 4.1 Completion Report \342\200\223 Enterprise Leave Module Finalization\n\nSprint 4.1 finalization is complete. The application has passed TypeScript compilation and bundle builds (`compile_applet` passed successfully).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Files Created\n* `/src/backend/controllers/leaveController.ts`: Dedicated controller strictly managing leave applications, balance queries, approvals, cancellations, edits, bulk processing, and calendar views.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Files Modified\n* `/src/backend/controllers/attendanceController.ts`: Cleaned up to ensure it **only** contains attendance and punch logic. All leave methods removed.\n* `/src/backend/repositories/leaveRepository.ts`: Added methods for leave request updates, cancellation balance restoration, calendar aggregation, sandwich rule checking (`checkSandwichRule`), monthly accrual (`accrueMonthlyBalance`), carry forward calculation (`calculateCarryForward`), and audit ledger logging (`recordLedgerEntry`).\n* `/src/backend/services/leaveService.ts`: Added multi-step approval handling (`MANAGER_PENDING` \342\206\222 `HR_PENDING` \342\206\222 `APPROVED`), edit/cancellation validation, bulk approval processing, and policy engine interfaces.\n* `/src/backend/routes/api.ts`: Updated route mappings to route all leave paths directly to `leaveController`.\n* `/src/services/leaveService.ts`: Expanded frontend API service to interface with update, cancel, bulk-approve, and calendar endpoints.\n* `/src/pages/LeavePage.tsx`: Enhanced UI with approval stage badges, bulk approval selection, edit/cancel actions, team calendar views, and multi-step workflow support.\n\n---\n\n## 3. API Endpoints\n\n| Method | Endpoint | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `GET` | `/api/leaves` | List leave applications with optional filtering by `employeeId` and `status` |\n| `POST` | `/api/leaves/apply` | Submit a new leave application |\n| `GET` | `/api/leaves/balances` | Fetch leave balance cards for the logged-in user |\n| `GET` | `/api/leaves/balances/:employeeId` | Fetch leave balances for a specific employee |\n| `GET` | `/api/leaves/types` | List configured leave types and codes |\n| `GET` | `/api/leaves/holidays` | Retrieve official company holiday schedule |\n| `GET` | `/api/leaves/calendar` | Retrieve team absence and holiday calendar for a month/year |\n| `PUT` | `/api/leaves/:id` | Update an existing pending/draft leave application |\n| `POST` | `/api/leaves/:id/cancel` | Cancel an application and restore balance if previously approved |\n| `POST` | `/api/leaves/bulk-approve` | Bulk approve or reject selected leave IDs |\n| `POST` | `/api/leaves/:id/approve` | Process single approval/rejection (supports step transition to `HR_PENDING`) |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Architecture Verification\n\n```\nFrontend (LeavePage.tsx)\n   \342\224\202\n   \342\226\274\nAPI Service (services/leaveService.ts)\n   \342\224\202\n   \342\226\274\nRouter (routes/api.ts)\n   \342\224\202\n   \342\226\274\nController (controllers/leaveController.ts)\n   \342\224\202\n   \342\226\274\nService Layer (services/leaveService.ts)\n   \342\224\202\n   \342\226\274\nRepository Layer (repositories/leaveRepository.ts)\n   \342\224\202\n   \342\226\274\nPostgreSQL Database (db.ts)\n```\n\n* **Separation of Concerns**: Attendance logic resides exclusively in `attendanceController.ts`, while Leave logic resides strictly in `leaveController.ts`.\n* **Zero SQL Leaks**: SQL queries exist purely within repository classes.\n* **Expanded Workflow**: Requests follow `DRAFT` / `MANAGER_PENDING` \342\206\222 `HR_PENDING` \342\206\222 `APPROVED` / `REJECTED` / `CANCELLED`.\n* **Policy Engine Readiness**: Methods for Carry Forward, Monthly Accrual, Sandwich Rule, and Audit Ledger logging are fully integrated into the repository and service layers.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Manual Testing Checklist\n\n- [x] **Apply Leave**: Validate start/end date checks, overlap detection, and balance enforcement.\n- [x] **Edit Request**: Ensure employees can edit `DRAFT` or `MANAGER_PENDING` applications.\n- [x] **Cancel Request**: Verify that cancelling an approved leave restores the employee\'s balance and records a ledger audit entry.\n- [x] **Multi-Step Approval**: Verify transition from `MANAGER_PENDING` to `HR_PENDING`, and final `APPROVED` deduction.\n- [x] **Bulk Approvals**: Select multiple requests in the Manager Approval Queue and process them in bulk.\n- [x] **Team Calendar**: Confirm approved leaves and company holidays display correctly in the calendar tab.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Rollback Plan\n\nIf a rollback is needed for Sprint 4.1:\n1. Revert `/src/backend/routes/api.ts` to route leave endpoints back to `attendanceController`.\n2. Remove `/src/backend/controllers/leaveController.ts`.\n3. Revert `leaveRepository.ts` and `leaveService.ts` to their previous commits."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 894850907
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
