    user_response: "You previously generated database_v2.\n\nDO NOT regenerate it.\n\nInstead, refactor the existing implementation.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\ndatabase_v2 MUST become a REAL PostgreSQL implementation.\n\nRemove ALL dependencies on:\n\n@electric-sql/pglite\nPGlite\nnew PGlite()\n\nReplace everything with the official PostgreSQL driver:\n\nimport { Pool, PoolClient } from \"pg\";\n\nRequirements:\n\n1. Rewrite connection.ts\n\n- Use Pool\n- Read credentials from .env\n\nDB_HOST\nDB_PORT\nDB_NAME\nDB_USER\nDB_PASSWORD\n\n- Support connection pooling\n- Support transactions\n- Support health check\n- Support graceful shutdown\n\n2. Rewrite every file inside database_v2\n\nschema.ts\nseed.ts\nindexes.ts\nconstraints.ts\nfunctions.ts\ntriggers.ts\nviews.ts\ntransactions.ts\naudit.ts\n\nThey must NOT receive a PGlite instance.\n\nInstead they should internally use the shared PostgreSQL Pool.\n\nExample:\n\nawait db.query(...)\n\nNOT\n\nawait db.exec(...)\n\n3. Rewrite transactions\n\nDo NOT use\n\nBEGIN\nCOMMIT\nROLLBACK\n\nthrough db.exec()\n\nInstead use\n\nconst client = await pool.connect()\n\nBEGIN\n\nCOMMIT\n\nROLLBACK\n\nclient.release()\n\n4. Remove every import of\n\n@electric-sql/pglite\n\n5. Remove every reference to\n\nPGlite\n\n6. Remove every\n\nnew PGlite()\n\n7. Remove every\n\ninstance.exec()\n\nReplace with PostgreSQL query execution.\n\n8. Replace health checks with\n\nSELECT version();\n\n9. Ensure the entire project compiles.\n\n10. Preserve every table, migration, constraint, trigger, index and seed already generated.\n\nThis is a refactor only.\n\nDo not redesign the architecture.\n\nOutput production-ready PostgreSQL code."
    items {
      text: "You previously generated database_v2.\n\nDO NOT regenerate it.\n\nInstead, refactor the existing implementation.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\ndatabase_v2 MUST become a REAL PostgreSQL implementation.\n\nRemove ALL dependencies on:\n\n@electric-sql/pglite\nPGlite\nnew PGlite()\n\nReplace everything with the official PostgreSQL driver:\n\nimport { Pool, PoolClient } from \"pg\";\n\nRequirements:\n\n1. Rewrite connection.ts\n\n- Use Pool\n- Read credentials from .env\n\nDB_HOST\nDB_PORT\nDB_NAME\nDB_USER\nDB_PASSWORD\n\n- Support connection pooling\n- Support transactions\n- Support health check\n- Support graceful shutdown\n\n2. Rewrite every file inside database_v2\n\nschema.ts\nseed.ts\nindexes.ts\nconstraints.ts\nfunctions.ts\ntriggers.ts\nviews.ts\ntransactions.ts\naudit.ts\n\nThey must NOT receive a PGlite instance.\n\nInstead they should internally use the shared PostgreSQL Pool.\n\nExample:\n\nawait db.query(...)\n\nNOT\n\nawait db.exec(...)\n\n3. Rewrite transactions\n\nDo NOT use\n\nBEGIN\nCOMMIT\nROLLBACK\n\nthrough db.exec()\n\nInstead use\n\nconst client = await pool.connect()\n\nBEGIN\n\nCOMMIT\n\nROLLBACK\n\nclient.release()\n\n4. Remove every import of\n\n@electric-sql/pglite\n\n5. Remove every reference to\n\nPGlite\n\n6. Remove every\n\nnew PGlite()\n\n7. Remove every\n\ninstance.exec()\n\nReplace with PostgreSQL query execution.\n\n8. Replace health checks with\n\nSELECT version();\n\n9. Ensure the entire project compiles.\n\n10. Preserve every table, migration, constraint, trigger, index and seed already generated.\n\nThis is a refactor only.\n\nDo not redesign the architecture.\n\nOutput production-ready PostgreSQL code."
