  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Project Changes**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that the initial compilation ran without a hitch! Zero errors is always a good sign. Now, I\'m shifting focus to a thorough review of the requested changes. Specifically, I\'m meticulously analyzing the alterations to `connection.ts`, including the new `pg` library integration and environment variable utilization. The goal is complete alignment with user directives.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have refactored the `database_v2` module into a native PostgreSQL implementation using the official `pg` (`node-postgres`) driver.\n\n### **Key Accomplishments**\n\n1. **PostgreSQL Driver Migration & Connection Pool (`connection.ts`)**:\n   - Replaced `PGlite` with `pg.Pool` and `pg.PoolClient`.\n   - Configured credentials to read dynamically from `.env` (`DB_HOST`, `DB_PORT`, `DB_NAME`, `DB_USER`, `DB_PASSWORD`).\n   - Implemented transaction management using isolated pool clients with explicit `BEGIN`, `COMMIT`, `ROLLBACK`, and `finally { client.release() }`.\n   - Updated the health check mechanism to execute `SELECT version();`.\n   - Added pool configuration options and graceful shutdown capabilities (`pool.end()`).\n\n2. **Refactored `database_v2` Architecture**:\n   - **`schema.ts`**: Replaced all `PGlite` references with `dbConnectionV2.query(...)` for DDL statement execution.\n   - **`seed.ts`**: Replaced all seed query methods to use the shared PostgreSQL connection pool.\n   - **`indexes.ts`**: Converted index initializations to use native PostgreSQL pool execution.\n   - **`constraints.ts`**: Converted constraint checks and modifications to use native PostgreSQL pool execution.\n   - **`functions.ts` & `triggers.ts`**: Replaced stored procedure and trigger creation logic with native PostgreSQL pool execution.\n   - **`views.ts`**: Converted enterprise views to run on the shared pool.\n   - **`transactions.ts`**: Updated transaction services to acquire client connections from the pool with complete error handling and connection releasing.\n   - **`audit.ts`**: Configured audit logging to utilize the native `pg` pool.\n\n3. **Environment & Verification**:\n   - Added default PostgreSQL configuration variables to `.env.example`.\n   - Cleaned up dependency references and verified that both type checking (`lint_applet`) and production compilation (`compile_applet`) pass cleanly."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 754612012
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
